Subject: [PATCH 1/4] lightbulb F1 checkpoint
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Save-before-effect checkpoint interface, inert by default (spec 02 §4.1).
agent/lb_checkpoint.py: Decision (proceed/refuse/replay), ToolRef, install(),
before_tool(), tool_committed(). With agent._lb_checkpoint unset every function
returns immediately. A callback that raises or exceeds timeout_s refuses the
call (fail closed) and records agent._lb_checkpoint_failed; unlike
pre_tool_call hooks its failure is never swallowed into "proceed".

Scope is before_tool + tool_committed only; before_model/model_accepted are cut
until a consumer exists. Which tools pay for an ack is the callback's policy
(contracts-v2 §8: external, irreversible effects only).

Also records the golden transcript of a stubbed two-tool turn at the
unpatched pin (tests/agent/fixtures/lb_golden_tool_turn.json).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
